WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.431
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:05.731 --> 00:00:08.920
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:15.089
Unit one: Second Conditional. Today you will talk about imaginary and unlikely situations.

4
00:00:15.389 --> 00:00:18.169
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:22.343
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.183 --> 00:00:24.196
If I were.

7
00:00:25.183 --> 00:00:28.506
If I were means the usual form for imagining being someone.

8
00:00:29.117 --> 00:00:31.105
If I were you, I would apply.

9
00:00:31.717 --> 00:00:34.775
Your turn. Say: If I were.

10
00:00:37.633 --> 00:00:38.542
If I were.

11
00:00:39.283 --> 00:00:39.959
Would.

12
00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:43.739
Would means the result of an imaginary condition.

13
00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:45.804
I would move abroad.

14
00:00:46.417 --> 00:00:49.127
Your turn. Say: Would.

15
00:00:51.967 --> 00:00:52.619
Would.

16
00:00:53.383 --> 00:00:54.501
Hypothetical.

17
00:00:55.517 --> 00:00:58.085
Hypothetical means imagined, not real.

18
00:00:58.683 --> 00:01:00.358
A hypothetical case.

19
00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:03.893
Your turn. Say: Hypothetical.

20
00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:08.001
Hypothetical.

21
00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:10.227
Unreal present.

22
00:01:11.217 --> 00:01:14.656
Unreal present means a present situation that is not true.

23
00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:16.890
It is an unreal present.

24
00:01:17.483 --> 00:01:20.449
Your turn. Say: Unreal present.

25
00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:25.044
Unreal present.

26
00:01:25.783 --> 00:01:26.970
Imaginary.

27
00:01:27.983 --> 00:01:30.633
Imaginary means existing only in the mind.

28
00:01:31.217 --> 00:01:32.752
An imaginary friend.

29
00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:35.979
Your turn. Say: Imaginary.

30
00:01:38.833 --> 00:01:39.939
Imaginary.

31
00:01:40.683 --> 00:01:41.557
Wish.

32
00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:45.211
Wish means to want something different from reality.

33
00:01:45.817 --> 00:01:47.329
I wish I had more time.

34
00:01:47.917 --> 00:01:50.035
Your turn. Say: Wish.

35
00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:53.564
Wish.

36
00:01:54.317 --> 00:01:55.329
Unlikely.

37
00:01:56.317 --> 00:01:58.328
Unlikely means not probable.

38
00:01:58.917 --> 00:02:00.312
Rain is unlikely.

39
00:02:00.917 --> 00:02:03.627
Your turn. Say: Unlikely.

40
00:02:06.467 --> 00:02:07.456
Unlikely.

41
00:02:08.217 --> 00:02:09.253
Suppose.

42
00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:12.935
Suppose means to imagine as a possibility.

43
00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:15.271
Suppose you won the lottery.

44
00:02:15.883 --> 00:02:18.652
Your turn. Say: Suppose.

45
00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:22.640
Suppose.

46
00:02:23.433 --> 00:02:27.061
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:27.917 --> 00:02:31.475
Visal, suppose you won a million dollars. What would you do?

48
00:02:32.583 --> 00:02:48.985
If I won a million dollars, I would invest half of it and travel with the rest. The second conditional is if + past simple, would + base verb. It describes an imaginary or unlikely present or future situation.

49
00:02:50.083 --> 00:02:51.967
Why is the verb in the past?

50
00:02:53.083 --> 00:03:03.956
The past tense marks distance from reality, not past time. We use were for all persons in formal English: If I were you, I would apply.

51
00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:06.492
Can would be replaced?

52
00:03:07.583 --> 00:03:18.830
Yes. Could and might show ability or weaker possibility: If I had a car, I could drive to work, or I might visit you. But never put would in the if-clause.

53
00:03:19.967 --> 00:03:21.397
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:27.779
Grammar focus: Second conditional: If plus past simple, would plus base verb.

55
00:03:28.079 --> 00:03:29.301
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:30.017 --> 00:03:33.317
If I won a million dollars, I would invest half of it.

57
00:03:34.217 --> 00:03:36.437
If I were you, I would apply for the job.

58
00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:40.127
Suppose you had a car, you could visit more often.

59
00:03:41.067 --> 00:03:50.107
If + past simple, would / could / might + base verb for unreal or unlikely situations. Say if I were. Suppose and imagine can replace if.

60
00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:54.466
Be careful! Don't say: If I would win, I would travel.

61
00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:59.189
Say: If I won, I would travel.

62
00:03:59.489 --> 00:04:01.640
Use the past simple in the if-clause.

63
00:04:02.433 --> 00:04:05.306
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:07.368
What Would You Do?.

65
00:04:07.668 --> 00:04:10.527
If I won a million dollars, I would invest half of it.

66
00:04:11.533 --> 00:04:14.589
I would also travel to every continent I have never seen.

67
00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:18.633
If I were the mayor, I could change the city's transport.

68
00:04:19.633 --> 00:04:23.398
These scenarios are hypothetical, because they are unlikely to happen.

69
00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:27.735
Suppose everyone recycled; our planet would be much cleaner.

70
00:04:28.833 --> 00:04:32.812
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:33.650 --> 00:04:36.079
If I blank rich, I would help more people.

72
00:04:36.379 --> 00:04:39.266
A, am. B, were. C, will be.

73
00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:44.544
The answer is B: were.

74
00:04:45.683 --> 00:04:47.903
She blank travel more if she had time.

75
00:04:48.203 --> 00:04:51.125
A, would. B, will. C, is.

76
00:04:54.667 --> 00:04:56.109
The answer is A: would.

77
00:04:57.250 --> 00:04:59.505
Which sentence is a second conditional?

78
00:04:59.805 --> 00:05:06.698
A, If it rains, we will stay.. B, If I had wings, I would fly.. C, If you heat ice, it melts..

79
00:05:10.233 --> 00:05:13.127
The answer is B: If I had wings, I would fly..

80
00:05:14.283 --> 00:05:15.540
Which is correct?

81
00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:22.280
A, If I would know, I would tell you.. B, If I knew, I would tell you.. C, If I know, I would tell you..

82
00:05:25.833 --> 00:05:28.808
The answer is B: If I knew, I would tell you..

83
00:05:29.950 --> 00:05:32.902
According to the reading, what would the mayor change?

84
00:05:33.202 --> 00:05:36.878
A, transport. B, taxes. C, schools.

85
00:05:40.433 --> 00:05:43.129
The answer is A: transport.

86
00:05:44.333 --> 00:05:47.322
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:48.183 --> 00:05:51.425
Complete: If I could change one thing about my school, I would...

88
00:06:00.217 --> 00:06:01.636
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:01.936 --> 00:06:16.711
If I could change one thing about my school, I would make the library bigger. If students had more space to read, they would enjoy studying more. I use the second conditional because the situation is imaginary.

90
00:06:17.011 --> 00:06:18.814
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:19.717 --> 00:06:27.187
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and second conditional: if plus past simple, would plus base verb.

92
00:06:27.487 --> 00:06:32.485
Today's value is reasoned judgment. Weigh the evidence before you decide what to believe.

93
00:06:32.785 --> 00:06:35.170
See you in Unit two. Goodbye!

94
00:06:35.470 --> 00:06:38.424
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

